---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Support — AutoLog"
  description="Adapters, protocol timing, codes, EVs, battery drain, and where your data lives — six questions, answered straight."
>
  <div class="page-column">
    <div class="head">
      <h1>Support</h1>
      <p class="sub">Six questions, answered straight.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq">
      <details class="panel faq-item">
        <summary>
          <span class="q">Which adapters work?</span>
          <span class="caret" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <p class="a">
          A Bluetooth LE ELM327, roughly $15. WiFi-only adapters won't pair;
          the app talks BLE only.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="panel faq-item" open>
        <summary>
          <span class="q"
            >Why does the first connection to an older car take a while?</span
          >
          <span class="caret" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <p class="a">
          Older cars talk on the K-line, ISO 9141-2, and the protocol search
          is slow by design. The adapter tries each protocol in turn until
          the car answers. The 2002 Miata in the test fleet takes its time
          too. Give the first connection half a minute; the ones after are
          quicker.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="panel faq-item" open>
        <summary>
          <span class="q">Does it clear codes?</span>
          <span class="caret" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <p class="a">
          No. Ever. AutoLog reads live data and reports the faults it sees.
          It never clears a code and never writes anything to the car.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="panel faq-item">
        <summary>
          <span class="q">Does it work with EVs and hybrids?</span>
          <span class="caret" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <p class="a">
          Yes. EVs and hybrids expose fewer PIDs over OBD2, so the app leans
          on the signals each car actually broadcasts, plus GPS, to keep
          trips accurate. Nothing invented, nothing assumed.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="panel faq-item">
        <summary>
          <span class="q">Will it drain the car battery?</span>
          <span class="caret" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <p class="a">
          No, not in normal use. The adapter draws a trickle from the OBD
          port, the same as any dash accessory. Unplug it if the car sits
          parked for weeks.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="panel faq-item">
        <summary>
          <span class="q">Where does my data live?</span>
          <span class="caret" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <p class="a">
          On the phone. Trips, stats, and vehicle data are stored locally.
          No account, no server, nothing leaves the device except two
          silent lookups covered on the privacy page.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>

    <div class="panel contact">
      <p class="contact-line">Still stuck? Write to the engineer.</p>
      <!-- TODO: dedicated address -->
      <p class="contact-email">hello@&hellip;</p>
    </div>

    <p class="build-marker">TESTFLIGHT BUILD 12</p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-column {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 100px 24px 40px;
  }

  .head {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 680px;
    padding-bottom: 44px;
  }

  .head h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 44px;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-display);
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .sub {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .faq {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .faq-item {
    width: 100%;
  }

  .faq-item summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 20px;
    padding: 22px 26px;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .faq-item summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .faq-item summary:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-amber);
    outline-offset: -2px;
    border-radius: var(--panel-radius);
  }

  .faq-item .q {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 24px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: rgba(var(--color-bone-rgb), 0.92);
  }

  .faq-item .a {
    padding: 0 60px 26px 26px;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 24px;
    color: rgba(var(--color-bone-rgb), 0.6);
  }

  .caret {
    position: relative;
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .caret::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    margin: auto;
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    border-right: 1.5px solid var(--text-muted);
    border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--text-muted);
    transform: translateY(-2px) rotate(45deg);
    transition: transform 0.2s var(--ease-spring);
  }

  details[open] .caret::before {
    transform: translateY(1px) rotate(225deg);
  }

  .contact {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 20px;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 680px;
    margin-top: 36px;
    padding: 26px;
    border-color: rgba(200, 127, 60, 0.35);
  }

  .contact-line {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 17px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: rgba(var(--color-bone-rgb), 0.92);
  }

  .contact-email {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .build-marker {
    padding: 72px 0 24px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.24em;
    color: var(--text-faint);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .page-column {
      padding: 64px 24px 30px;
    }

    .head {
      gap: 10px;
      padding-bottom: 32px;
    }

    .head h1 {
      font-size: 34px;
    }

    .sub {
      font-size: 15px;
    }

    .faq {
      gap: 10px;
    }

    .faq-item summary {
      padding: 18px 20px;
    }

    .faq-item .q {
      font-size: 15.5px;
      line-height: 22px;
    }

    .faq-item .a {
      padding: 0 20px 20px;
      font-size: 14.5px;
      line-height: 23px;
    }

    .contact {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 10px;
      margin-top: 28px;
      padding: 22px 20px;
    }

    .contact-line {
      font-size: 16px;
    }

    .build-marker {
      padding: 56px 0 10px;
    }
  }
</style>
